:name: Arduino UNO R4 WiFi (RA4M1 side) with a scripted ESP32-S3
:description: Runs a sketch ELF on Renode's RA4M1 model; Serial (SCI9) goes to $serial_out, and fake_esp32.py answers the AT link (Serial2 = SCI1).

# Required variables (set them before including this file):
#   $elf         the sketch ELF from arduino-cli compile --output-dir
#   $serial_out  file that receives everything the sketch prints on Serial
#   $at_tx_out   file that receives every byte the RA4M1 sends on the AT link
#   $sci_model   @path of UnoR4_SCI.cs
#   $platform    @path of uno_r4_wifi.repl

include $sci_model
mach create "uno_r4_wifi"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $platform

sysbus LoadELF $elf
# The Arduino bootloader owns 0x0000-0x3FFF; the sketch's vector table is at 0x4000.
cpu VectorTableOffset 0x4000

sysbus.sci9 CreateFileBackend $serial_out true
sysbus.sci1 CreateFileBackend $at_tx_out true
# The caller then attaches the ESP32-S3 stand-in (Renode does not expand $variables inside the
# hook's quoted Python, so the path to fake_esp32.py is written out literally by run.sh):
#   sysbus.sci1 AddLineHook "AT" "import sys; sys.path.append(r'<dir>') if r'<dir>' not in sys.path else None; import fake_esp32; fake_esp32.on_line(machine, uart, line)"
